WEBVTT

1
00:01:34.458 --> 00:01:36.583
Glory to Goddess Kali!

2
00:02:19.042 --> 00:02:20.202
The cloth. Hand me the cloth.

3
00:02:25.542 --> 00:02:27.042
- What is it?
- It's a boy.

4
00:02:27.333 --> 00:02:28.208
Wait.

5
00:02:28.292 --> 00:02:30.625
She's having twins.
The other child is on the way.

6
00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.208
Master. Master.

7
00:02:51.333 --> 00:02:52.583
It's a boy.

8
00:02:53.625 --> 00:02:56.375
But… she's having twins.

9
00:02:56.458 --> 00:02:57.579
Another child is on the way.

10
00:03:13.458 --> 00:03:16.333
It's a boy.
Thank you, Goddess!

11
00:03:16.417 --> 00:03:17.875
Thank you, Goddess!

12
00:03:17.958 --> 00:03:19.279
This is all that was left to see.

13
00:03:19.625 --> 00:03:21.208
How can a woman perform the ritual?

14
00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:24.000
You are the village chief's son.

15
00:03:24.208 --> 00:03:25.708
You come from a high-caste lineage.

16
00:03:25.917 --> 00:03:27.167
Such a prestigious ritual.

17
00:03:27.917 --> 00:03:30.277
You should have had the honor
of leading this sacred ritual.

18
00:03:31.708 --> 00:03:34.208
Joydev, how could
your father allow this?

19
00:03:34.292 --> 00:03:35.500
Father couldn't interfere.

20
00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:38.500
She claimed Goddess Kali
appeared in her dreams.

21
00:03:39.125 --> 00:03:40.851
So, she was given
the honor of performing the ritual.

22
00:03:40.875 --> 00:03:41.917
It's a tradition.

23
00:04:30.958 --> 00:04:31.958
It's a girl.

24
00:05:06.625 --> 00:05:07.667
Shuvankar.

25
00:05:12.417 --> 00:05:14.667
My daughter… have mercy on her.

26
00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.625
Return my daughter to me.

27
00:05:17.833 --> 00:05:19.833
My daughter…
Return my daughter to me.

28
00:05:20.250 --> 00:05:23.667
Give her... No. No.

29
00:05:23.750 --> 00:05:24.875
She is my daughter.

30
00:05:25.583 --> 00:05:28.292
She is your daughter.
Don't take her away.

31
00:05:28.375 --> 00:05:29.375
No!

32
00:05:29.708 --> 00:05:33.625
No, don't do it. Don't.

33
00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:36.667
Let me go!
Leave me! Let me go!

34
00:05:37.292 --> 00:05:38.625
Don't take her away.

35
00:06:34.875 --> 00:06:38.458
When the demon will spread its sins,

36
00:06:38.833 --> 00:06:42.042
the tears of the daughter will
seep into the soil as blood,

37
00:06:42.125 --> 00:06:45.833
the blood of the daughter
will annihilate the demon.

38
00:07:28.875 --> 00:07:29.875
<i>Women empowerment.</i>

39
00:07:30.500 --> 00:07:32.667
Feminine energy is represented by…

40
00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:34.000
Seven Goddesses.

41
00:07:34.292 --> 00:07:36.833
And leading them is Goddess Kali.

42
00:07:37.708 --> 00:07:39.542
Ambika ma'am, who is that?

43
00:07:41.125 --> 00:07:43.250
That… is Raktabij.

44
00:07:43.958 --> 00:07:45.458
A mythological demon,

45
00:07:46.083 --> 00:07:49.292
who defeated all the Gods
and cast them out of Heaven.

46
00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.833
Gods? Defeated by a demon?

47
00:07:52.417 --> 00:07:55.542
At the start of the war,
it was just him. Alone.

48
00:07:56.333 --> 00:07:58.292
But whenever the
Gods struck him down,

49
00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:00.875
and his blood would fall on earth…

50
00:08:01.375 --> 00:08:06.375
A new demon rose
from every drop of his blood.

51
00:08:06.958 --> 00:08:09.500
Raktabij's blood
kept falling on earth,

52
00:08:09.667 --> 00:08:11.042
and the demons kept multiplying.

53
00:08:11.333 --> 00:08:13.542
Forming an army.

54
00:08:13.958 --> 00:08:15.042
What happened next, ma'am?

55
00:08:15.625 --> 00:08:19.083
Then the Gods sought help
from Goddess Parvati.

56
00:08:19.917 --> 00:08:23.792
She was a mother.
All the Gods were like her children.

57
00:08:24.458 --> 00:08:28.250
And what do mothers do
when children are in danger?

58
00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:30.667
She becomes dangerous too.

59
00:08:31.625 --> 00:08:32.625
Exactly.

60
00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:37.500
So, in a fit of rage, Goddess Parvati
transformed into Goddess Kali.

61
00:08:38.292 --> 00:08:40.292
Dangerous. Powerful.

62
00:08:41.083 --> 00:08:45.000
And along with the seven Goddesses,
lay siege on Raktabij.

63
00:08:45.208 --> 00:08:48.583
Goddess Kali would behead
Raktabij with her axe

64
00:08:48.833 --> 00:08:53.875
and would drink his blood
before it could fall on earth.

65
00:08:54.083 --> 00:08:59.417
By doing so, one by one, she destroyed
every incarnation of Raktabij.

66
00:09:03.500 --> 00:09:04.667
Thank you so much.

67
00:09:04.750 --> 00:09:06.550
- Come, children. Follow me.
- Thank you, ma'am.

68
00:09:06.708 --> 00:09:08.208
- Come. This way…
- Let's go…

69
00:09:08.292 --> 00:09:09.625
Let's go to the next section…

70
00:09:11.208 --> 00:09:13.250
Very impressive presentation, I must say.

71
00:09:14.417 --> 00:09:15.417
Thank you.

72
00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:17.711
The way you explained
everything with such passion

73
00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:19.500
I didn't want to
take my eyes off you.

74
00:09:20.542 --> 00:09:22.417
By the way, I am Shuvankar Das Gupta.

75
00:09:23.125 --> 00:09:24.708
Nice to meet you, Mr. Das Gupta.

76
00:09:26.125 --> 00:09:30.417
But what if your wife finds out
that you are flirting with me?

77
00:09:32.125 --> 00:09:34.417
Well, in that case,
I'll tell her she can't blame me.

78
00:09:35.125 --> 00:09:37.458
Your face is quite
similar to my wife's.

79
00:09:39.625 --> 00:09:42.292
That is so lame. So lame.

80
00:09:42.583 --> 00:09:43.625
Where is Shweta?

81
00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:45.000
Over there.

82
00:09:55.417 --> 00:09:56.417
Dad…

83
00:09:57.208 --> 00:09:58.729
Diwali vacations
are around the corner.

84
00:09:59.292 --> 00:10:01.750
And my literature teacher has told us

85
00:10:02.125 --> 00:10:06.458
to travel to our respective
village and find an old story.

86
00:10:06.792 --> 00:10:10.458
The best one will be adapted
into the school play this year.

87
00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:12.360
You just made that up, didn't you?

88
00:10:12.542 --> 00:10:14.083
You can call the teacher.

89
00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:18.167
Why don't we take a trip
to Shimla this year?

90
00:10:18.333 --> 00:10:19.333
Excellent idea!

91
00:10:19.625 --> 00:10:21.875
Snow-clad valleys. Enchanting views.

92
00:10:22.667 --> 00:10:23.667
What do you think, dear?

93
00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.333
Forget it, Dad.

94
00:10:25.833 --> 00:10:27.458
You're trying to change the topic again.

95
00:10:27.625 --> 00:10:29.875
You know where my heart is set to go.

96
00:10:30.708 --> 00:10:34.208
Chandarpur is still stuck
in the stone age like me, dear.

97
00:10:34.292 --> 00:10:35.792
There's no network or internet.

98
00:10:35.875 --> 00:10:38.500
- Exactly.
- Yes. You'll get bored in two days.

99
00:10:39.667 --> 00:10:41.547
Pick any other city,
sweetheart, we'll go there.

100
00:10:42.083 --> 00:10:44.875
I just don't understand
what is wrong with Chandarpur.

101
00:10:44.958 --> 00:10:46.583
Why can't I go there?

102
00:10:50.250 --> 00:10:51.917
<i>We will have to tell
her sooner or later.</i>

103
00:10:56.292 --> 00:10:57.500
She is only 12-years-old.

104
00:10:58.875 --> 00:10:59.875
She won't understand.

105
00:11:04.333 --> 00:11:05.333
She will.

106
00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:10.083
And the sooner the better.

107
00:11:12.417 --> 00:11:13.417
I guess, you are right.

108
00:11:15.167 --> 00:11:16.167
Maybe for the first time.

109
00:11:19.833 --> 00:11:22.042
Now, stop smoking and come inside.

110
00:11:22.125 --> 00:11:23.542
- Come. Please!
- Coming. Coming.

111
00:11:24.292 --> 00:11:25.292
Go ahead.

112
00:11:30.917 --> 00:11:31.917
Yes, Bikash. What is it?

113
00:11:57.917 --> 00:12:00.167
What happened?
Is everything alright?

114
00:12:02.292 --> 00:12:03.625
I got a call from Chandarpur.

115
00:12:05.833 --> 00:12:06.917
Dad passed away.

116
00:12:09.042 --> 00:12:10.042
I am…

117
00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:12.250
I am so sorry.

118
00:12:15.625 --> 00:12:17.083
I need to leave right away, Ambi.

119
00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:50.500
Chandarpur?

120
00:12:50.542 --> 00:12:51.542
Yes.

121
00:12:51.958 --> 00:12:53.167
Why didn't he tell me?

122
00:12:54.417 --> 00:12:55.292
I know why.

123
00:12:55.417 --> 00:12:57.583
He didn't tell me
because I would insist on going.

124
00:12:58.333 --> 00:13:01.042
It was an emergency, dear.
And you were sleeping.

125
00:13:01.542 --> 00:13:03.292
What was the emergency, Mom?

126
00:13:03.833 --> 00:13:05.958
He could have at least said bye.

127
00:13:08.042 --> 00:13:09.042
Well…

128
00:13:10.458 --> 00:13:13.250
Your grandpa…
He passed away.

129
00:13:14.167 --> 00:13:15.167
My grandpa?

130
00:13:16.083 --> 00:13:19.417
- You mean Dad's father.
- Yes.

131
00:13:19.583 --> 00:13:21.750
My grandpa was alive all these years,

132
00:13:22.375 --> 00:13:25.125
and neither of you ever told me.

133
00:13:28.083 --> 00:13:31.958
That means Grandpa didn't
know about me either.

134
00:13:33.167 --> 00:13:34.167
Right, Mom?

135
00:14:11.917 --> 00:14:13.667
I stayed back to meet you,
Joydev <i>da.</i>

136
00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:14.750
Is it?

137
00:14:15.250 --> 00:14:17.042
It wasn't your father's time to go.

138
00:14:18.042 --> 00:14:19.708
I was deeply hurt when he passed.

139
00:14:20.875 --> 00:14:22.333
Joydev <i>da,</i>

140
00:14:23.208 --> 00:14:26.042
can you suggest a good broker?

141
00:14:26.417 --> 00:14:27.917
Broker? Why?

142
00:14:29.708 --> 00:14:31.375
I want to sell this manor.

143
00:14:31.958 --> 00:14:32.958
But why?

144
00:14:33.125 --> 00:14:35.250
It's not just a manor,
it's your legacy.

145
00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:40.583
Our legacy has been a curse.

146
00:14:42.167 --> 00:14:44.500
And I've no interest
in taking care of such a legacy.

147
00:14:45.625 --> 00:14:47.184
That too, in a village infested by demons.

148
00:14:47.208 --> 00:14:49.542
Oh, that's history now!

149
00:14:50.500 --> 00:14:51.792
No one believes in it anymore.

150
00:14:52.333 --> 00:14:54.500
Children laugh at the lore of the <i>daitya.</i>

151
00:14:57.583 --> 00:14:58.583
Alright.

152
00:14:59.458 --> 00:15:00.708
I'll suggest you a good broker.

153
00:15:00.958 --> 00:15:02.167
But you must think this over.

154
00:15:03.625 --> 00:15:04.667
Wouldn't it be nice

155
00:15:05.583 --> 00:15:09.750
if your family gets to see your legacy?

156
00:15:09.833 --> 00:15:11.083
Your wife, your daughter.

157
00:15:11.292 --> 00:15:14.167
I don't have a daughter.
I have a son.

158
00:15:15.292 --> 00:15:17.000
No need to keep secrets from me.

159
00:15:17.083 --> 00:15:18.684
Your father told me about your daughter.

160
00:15:19.125 --> 00:15:20.292
But don't worry.

161
00:15:21.667 --> 00:15:24.542
No one in the village knows this but me.

162
00:15:29.417 --> 00:15:30.417
<i>Yes, Ambi. Tell me.</i>

163
00:15:30.750 --> 00:15:32.833
Yes, Shuv. Are you okay?

164
00:15:33.292 --> 00:15:35.583
Yes, I'm leaving in an hour.

165
00:15:36.333 --> 00:15:38.000
You drove for hours.

166
00:15:38.375 --> 00:15:40.458
<i>- Why don't you stay there tonight?</i>
- No, Ambi.

167
00:15:40.583 --> 00:15:42.584
I've no interest in staying
here even for a minute.

168
00:15:44.042 --> 00:15:45.208
I feel suffocated.

169
00:15:45.917 --> 00:15:47.708
<i>And we'll also sell this manor, Ambi.</i>

170
00:15:48.667 --> 00:15:50.875
<i>I don't want any ties to this place.</i>

171
00:15:51.458 --> 00:15:52.458
<i>Dada…</i>

172
00:15:53.125 --> 00:15:55.833
Ambi, I have the keys.
So you can sleep.

173
00:15:56.250 --> 00:15:57.250
I'll see you soon.

174
00:15:57.292 --> 00:15:59.167
Okay, bye.

175
00:16:01.792 --> 00:16:02.833
- Bikash.
<i>- Dada…</i>

176
00:16:03.333 --> 00:16:05.250
- Take care of Vimal <i>da.</i>
- Sure.

177
00:16:05.917 --> 00:16:07.917
- And call me if you need anything.
- Okay.

178
00:16:08.333 --> 00:16:09.333
<i>Dada!</i>

179
00:16:10.417 --> 00:16:11.292
<i>Dada…</i>

180
00:16:11.417 --> 00:16:12.667
Oh, God.

181
00:16:13.625 --> 00:16:15.458
- Did you get hurt?
- It's okay.

182
00:17:19.125 --> 00:17:20.125
COME CAREFULLY…

183
00:17:39.792 --> 00:17:41.708
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Hello, Ambi.

184
00:17:41.875 --> 00:17:43.875
Yes, Shuv.
Did you see the drawing?

185
00:17:43.958 --> 00:17:46.792
Yes. Where did Shweta see this face?

186
00:17:46.958 --> 00:17:48.958
<i>- Where did… she… see this face…</i>
- Hello.

187
00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.958
Hello. Ambi, can you hear me?

188
00:17:51.042 --> 00:17:52.500
<i>- Ambi.</i>
- Yes, Shuv.

189
00:17:52.833 --> 00:17:54.083
Hello, Ambi. Can you hear me?

190
00:17:54.375 --> 00:17:55.625
Where did Shweta see this face?

191
00:17:57.167 --> 00:17:58.917
Where has Shweta seen this face?

192
00:18:01.167 --> 00:18:02.958
Hello, Ambi. Can you hear me?

193
00:18:04.833 --> 00:18:06.292
I can't hear you. Shuv…

194
00:18:07.417 --> 00:18:08.417
Are you there?

195
00:18:17.417 --> 00:18:18.417
Hello.

196
00:18:19.750 --> 00:18:20.750
Hello, Ambi.

197
00:18:21.167 --> 00:18:22.042
Can you hear me?

198
00:18:22.125 --> 00:18:25.167
Hello, Ambi.
Hello, Ambi. Can you hear me?

199
00:18:25.250 --> 00:18:26.333
Ambi. Ambi.

200
00:18:27.333 --> 00:18:28.625
Hello. Hello.

201
00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.042
Ambi… Can you hear me?

202
00:18:31.125 --> 00:18:33.583
Hello. Ambi, can you hear me?

203
00:18:33.833 --> 00:18:34.833
Shit!

204
00:18:41.875 --> 00:18:42.875
Shit!

205
00:20:16.500 --> 00:20:17.542
He was exhausted.

206
00:20:18.000 --> 00:20:20.208
He had parked on the roadside to rest.

207
00:20:21.292 --> 00:20:23.417
Maybe his cigarette started the fire.

208
00:20:49.042 --> 00:20:50.122
Greetings, daughter-in-law.

209
00:20:51.167 --> 00:20:53.625
I am Joydev Bandhopadhyay.

210
00:20:53.708 --> 00:20:55.000
The village chief of Chandarpur.

211
00:20:56.333 --> 00:20:58.333
If you need anything,
don't hesitate to call.

212
00:20:59.083 --> 00:21:00.083
I am here for you.

213
00:21:00.458 --> 00:21:02.259
You have the support
of the entire Chandarpur.

214
00:21:04.750 --> 00:21:05.750
Yes.

215
00:21:07.000 --> 00:21:08.000
Take care.

216
00:21:08.625 --> 00:21:09.625
See you.

217
00:21:16.625 --> 00:21:17.625
Sweetheart,

218
00:21:18.375 --> 00:21:19.625
eat something.

219
00:21:21.042 --> 00:21:22.583
You haven't eaten since morning.

220
00:21:26.167 --> 00:21:27.625
At times like these, it's…

221
00:21:31.625 --> 00:21:34.250
- Necessary.
- You haven't eaten either.

222
00:21:45.042 --> 00:21:47.042
Come here. Come here.

223
00:21:53.208 --> 00:21:54.208
It's okay.

224
00:22:02.250 --> 00:22:03.583
I miss him, Mom.

225
00:22:07.333 --> 00:22:08.708
I miss him too.

226
00:22:24.583 --> 00:22:25.792
<i>Ambi.</i>

227
00:22:28.125 --> 00:22:29.667
<i>Ambi.</i>

228
00:22:30.875 --> 00:22:32.250
<i>Ambika.</i>

229
00:22:53.750 --> 00:22:55.875
Mom, call for you.

230
00:22:59.500 --> 00:23:00.500
Hello.

231
00:23:00.667 --> 00:23:02.208
Hello, Shweta dear.

232
00:23:02.417 --> 00:23:04.667
It's the village chief
speaking from Chandarpur.

233
00:23:04.917 --> 00:23:07.333
<i>Where is your mom?
Tell her I need to speak to her urgently.</i>

234
00:23:07.417 --> 00:23:08.417
Who is it?

235
00:23:09.083 --> 00:23:10.167
It's from Chandarpur.

236
00:23:12.875 --> 00:23:13.792
Hello.

237
00:23:13.875 --> 00:23:17.042
Hello, daughter-in-law. How are you?

238
00:23:17.167 --> 00:23:18.167
All good?

239
00:23:18.708 --> 00:23:19.792
Yes, all good.

240
00:23:20.333 --> 00:23:22.792
Tell me, was it something urgent?

241
00:23:22.875 --> 00:23:23.958
<i>Yes, dear.</i>

242
00:23:24.667 --> 00:23:27.375
<i>It's been three months
since Shuvankar passed away.</i>

243
00:23:27.625 --> 00:23:30.417
But something has been bothering me.

244
00:23:31.375 --> 00:23:33.500
Shuvankar said he
wanted to sell the manor.

245
00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:38.042
Yes, I know. He told me.

246
00:23:38.375 --> 00:23:40.125
<i>Great. Half the work's done then.</i>

247
00:23:40.417 --> 00:23:43.292
A broker is coming over the day
after tomorrow to look at the manor.

248
00:23:43.875 --> 00:23:46.500
If you could come here,
we could finish the paperwork.

249
00:23:46.917 --> 00:23:48.317
Day-after-tomorrow seems difficult.

250
00:23:49.500 --> 00:23:50.708
Why don't you handle it?

251
00:23:50.875 --> 00:23:53.208
<i>I'm ready to pay whatever
commission you want.</i>

252
00:23:53.292 --> 00:23:54.667
Please, daughter-in-law.

253
00:23:55.625 --> 00:23:58.292
You are misunderstanding me.

254
00:23:58.375 --> 00:24:00.875
<i>I just want Shuvankar's
final wish to be fulfilled,</i>

255
00:24:01.375 --> 00:24:03.292
so his soul can rest in peace.

256
00:24:03.375 --> 00:24:05.417
That's all I want. Nothing more.

257
00:24:06.917 --> 00:24:08.083
I will try.

258
00:24:08.542 --> 00:24:10.000
Alright. See you then.

259
00:24:11.917 --> 00:24:13.833
Are we going to Chandarpur?

260
00:24:15.833 --> 00:24:16.833
I am going.

261
00:24:18.042 --> 00:24:19.442
You'll be staying with Riti auntie.

262
00:24:20.958 --> 00:24:23.292
No, Mom. I am also coming along.

263
00:24:24.083 --> 00:24:26.375
- You can't come, dear.
- Why not?

264
00:24:27.333 --> 00:24:30.167
- You don't get it, it's...
- You don't get it, Mom.

265
00:24:30.417 --> 00:24:32.625
I cannot leave you alone.

266
00:24:33.375 --> 00:24:36.500
- It's only for two days.
- Even Dad went alone.

267
00:24:37.292 --> 00:24:38.625
Don't you understand?

268
00:24:39.167 --> 00:24:41.000
What if you also…

269
00:24:47.292 --> 00:24:49.083
I miss him so much, Mom.

270
00:24:50.083 --> 00:24:52.542
I couldn't even say
a proper goodbye to Dad.

271
00:24:54.292 --> 00:24:55.625
Please let me come along.

272
00:24:55.875 --> 00:25:00.458
And I promise I'll never
even mention Chandarpur after this.

273
00:25:04.708 --> 00:25:05.708
Okay.

274
00:25:11.667 --> 00:25:17.250
<i>When you are by my side
At every crossroads</i>

275
00:25:17.583 --> 00:25:22.375
<i>The path does not worry me</i>

276
00:25:23.500 --> 00:25:29.125
<i>I accept all the ups and downs</i>

277
00:25:29.583 --> 00:25:33.667
<i>When you are my companion</i>

278
00:25:34.333 --> 00:25:40.000
<i>You are my reason to smile</i>

279
00:25:40.500 --> 00:25:47.208
<i>Your existence
Is like my heartbeat</i>

280
00:25:47.292 --> 00:25:48.958
<i>O benefactor of mine</i>

281
00:25:49.958 --> 00:25:54.917
<i>O benefactor of mine
I exist when you do</i>

282
00:25:55.083 --> 00:26:01.042
<i>Tell me how am I going
To live without you</i>

283
00:26:01.958 --> 00:26:06.917
<i>O benefactor of mine
I exist when you do</i>

284
00:26:07.042 --> 00:26:13.958
<i>Tell me how am I going
To live without you</i>

285
00:26:47.667 --> 00:26:48.667
Mom!

286
00:26:56.792 --> 00:26:58.512
Constantly up to some mischief
all day long.

287
00:26:59.458 --> 00:27:02.042
- Couldn't you see the car coming?
- No, no…

288
00:27:02.292 --> 00:27:04.333
Don't scold her.
It was my fault. I am so sorry.

289
00:27:04.625 --> 00:27:05.625
Are you alright?

290
00:27:05.792 --> 00:27:06.792
Did you get hurt?

291
00:27:09.917 --> 00:27:10.917
What is your name?

292
00:27:11.250 --> 00:27:12.333
Deepika.

293
00:27:13.250 --> 00:27:14.250
Deepika,

294
00:27:15.292 --> 00:27:16.292
this is Shweta.

295
00:27:16.542 --> 00:27:17.542
Say hello to her.

296
00:27:20.375 --> 00:27:23.708
I am Bikash.
This is my wife Nandini.

297
00:27:25.833 --> 00:27:26.833
Come.

298
00:27:36.750 --> 00:27:38.250
This is my favorite chocolate.

299
00:27:51.125 --> 00:27:52.125
Wow.

300
00:27:53.958 --> 00:27:55.500
I love this place, Mom.

301
00:29:02.000 --> 00:29:03.000
Is that Grandpa?

302
00:29:05.792 --> 00:29:06.792
Yes.

303
00:29:08.042 --> 00:29:09.083
He is your grandpa.

304
00:29:10.708 --> 00:29:13.417
Sister, do you know,

305
00:29:13.833 --> 00:29:15.958
there are thirty rooms in this manor?

306
00:29:16.667 --> 00:29:17.667
That's a lie.

307
00:29:17.958 --> 00:29:18.958
Why would I lie?

308
00:29:19.667 --> 00:29:21.375
Let's count it. Come on.

309
00:29:34.042 --> 00:29:35.042
- Listen.
- Yes.

310
00:29:36.375 --> 00:29:37.833
Is she Shuvankar <i>da's</i> daughter?

311
00:29:38.583 --> 00:29:39.667
- But...
- Quiet. Quiet.

312
00:29:39.833 --> 00:29:40.833
Be quiet.

313
00:29:41.083 --> 00:29:42.083
Go and make some tea.

314
00:29:42.167 --> 00:29:43.708
- But…
- I said go make some tea.

315
00:29:45.333 --> 00:29:48.333
And that's room number eight and nine.

316
00:29:50.583 --> 00:29:51.583
Room number ten.

317
00:29:52.625 --> 00:29:53.833
Room number eleven.

318
00:29:55.375 --> 00:29:56.708
Room number twelve.

319
00:29:57.042 --> 00:29:58.042
- Bikash<i> da.</i>
- Yes?

320
00:29:58.375 --> 00:30:00.292
Why is the temple locked?

321
00:30:00.542 --> 00:30:01.583
Room number fourteen.

322
00:30:02.083 --> 00:30:04.000
- Now, let's go upstairs.
- Yes, let's go.

323
00:30:07.000 --> 00:30:08.958
It's been locked for forty years, sister.

324
00:30:09.917 --> 00:30:11.797
Goddess Kali hasn't appeared
in anyone's dreams.

325
00:30:12.542 --> 00:30:13.542
As in?

326
00:30:13.917 --> 00:30:15.125
It's a tradition, sister.

327
00:30:15.875 --> 00:30:18.417
When Goddess Kali appears
in someone's dreams,

328
00:30:18.833 --> 00:30:20.417
only then are the temple doors opened.

329
00:30:21.333 --> 00:30:24.083
And only the one who beholds
the Goddess in their dream

330
00:30:24.167 --> 00:30:26.083
gets the honor to perform the rituals.

331
00:30:28.833 --> 00:30:30.333
Such is Goddess Kali's divine play.

332
00:30:31.083 --> 00:30:33.375
She hasn't appeared in
anyone's dreams for forty years.

333
00:30:37.000 --> 00:30:38.440
How long have you been working here?

334
00:30:38.500 --> 00:30:40.083
We've been working
here for generations.

335
00:30:40.708 --> 00:30:43.042
My father served this
family for fifty years.

336
00:30:43.333 --> 00:30:45.667
When he fell sick
a couple of years ago,

337
00:30:46.083 --> 00:30:47.875
Nandini and I took his place.

338
00:30:49.500 --> 00:30:50.500
Fifty years!

339
00:30:52.667 --> 00:30:54.208
Can I meet your father?

340
00:30:54.917 --> 00:30:57.542
My father? But what's the point?

341
00:30:57.625 --> 00:30:59.250
He can't understand
a word anyone says.

342
00:30:59.333 --> 00:31:01.208
He just lies there.

343
00:31:02.125 --> 00:31:03.125
Okay, fine.

344
00:31:03.167 --> 00:31:06.042
Since you insist,
I'll take you to him.

345
00:31:06.375 --> 00:31:07.375
Father.

346
00:31:08.833 --> 00:31:11.833
Room number twenty-seven, twenty-eight.

347
00:31:13.083 --> 00:31:16.250
Room number twenty-nine
and that's thirty.

348
00:31:26.167 --> 00:31:27.167
Greetings.

349
00:31:27.875 --> 00:31:28.875
I am Ambika.

350
00:31:30.292 --> 00:31:31.417
Shuvankar's wife.

351
00:31:32.375 --> 00:31:35.750
You served our family
for so many years

352
00:31:36.583 --> 00:31:39.708
and I want to thank you for that.

353
00:31:43.583 --> 00:31:46.750
Grandpa. Look who's here.

354
00:31:47.708 --> 00:31:49.917
She's my friend. Take a look.

355
00:31:50.542 --> 00:31:51.542
Look.

356
00:31:52.375 --> 00:31:53.375
Take a look.

357
00:31:55.833 --> 00:31:57.792
See, that's my friend.

358
00:31:58.625 --> 00:31:59.625
See…

359
00:32:02.958 --> 00:32:03.958
Have you lost it?

360
00:32:07.208 --> 00:32:08.208
Is everything alright?

361
00:32:08.458 --> 00:32:10.500
Yes, sister.
Everything is alright.

362
00:32:11.042 --> 00:32:12.875
Come, I'll show you around the house.

363
00:32:20.333 --> 00:32:22.625
You seem to have become friends
with Deepika pretty soon.

364
00:32:22.917 --> 00:32:26.250
Yes, but I guess her mom
doesn't like me very much.

365
00:32:29.208 --> 00:32:31.875
- Do you need anything else, sister?
- No. Thanks.

366
00:32:42.833 --> 00:32:43.875
Was the food okay, sister?

367
00:32:44.250 --> 00:32:45.667
Yes, it was nice.

368
00:32:46.083 --> 00:32:48.500
Nandini is a very good cook.

369
00:32:52.083 --> 00:32:53.542
How did you like the food?

370
00:32:53.667 --> 00:32:54.667
It was nice.

371
00:32:57.208 --> 00:32:59.458
Bikash <i>da,</i> the broker
is arriving tomorrow morning.

372
00:33:00.125 --> 00:33:01.542
Inform me as soon as he does.

373
00:33:02.250 --> 00:33:03.250
Okay, sister.

374
00:33:06.042 --> 00:33:07.042
Goodnight.

375
00:33:12.125 --> 00:33:13.167
We are doomed.

376
00:33:13.625 --> 00:33:15.750
- Mom.
- Everything will fall apart.

377
00:33:16.833 --> 00:33:18.250
It's all going to go wrong.

378
00:33:18.500 --> 00:33:20.792
No one can escape this curse.

379
00:33:20.875 --> 00:33:22.125
Everyone is going to die.

380
00:33:22.333 --> 00:33:24.958
- Father, come.
- Everyone will die.

381
00:33:25.042 --> 00:33:26.184
- It will all go downhill.
- Father.

382
00:33:26.208 --> 00:33:28.750
Forgive him, sister.
He hasn't spoken for years.

383
00:33:28.958 --> 00:33:30.000
And now suddenly…

384
00:33:30.083 --> 00:33:33.542
- Everyone, leave.
- Father, let's go…

385
00:33:33.625 --> 00:33:36.917
- We're all going to die.
- Father…

386
00:33:43.417 --> 00:33:46.208
Mom, what was he saying?

387
00:33:47.875 --> 00:33:50.375
Nothing, dear. He's unwell.

388
00:33:51.625 --> 00:33:52.542
I know that, Mom.

389
00:33:52.625 --> 00:33:55.542
But what did he mean by what he said?

390
00:33:57.708 --> 00:34:01.958
That… Shweta, this is an unfamiliar place.

391
00:34:02.708 --> 00:34:05.375
So don't wander off without
telling your mom, okay?

392
00:34:05.875 --> 00:34:06.875
Very funny.

393
00:35:28.125 --> 00:35:30.417
- Hello. Hello.
- Hello, daughter-in-law.

394
00:35:30.500 --> 00:35:32.583
This is Satya Babu.
The agent.

395
00:35:32.833 --> 00:35:34.542
- I mean…
- Broker.

396
00:35:34.625 --> 00:35:36.208
- Broker.
- Hello.

397
00:35:36.750 --> 00:35:40.417
If you can get this sale done urgently…

398
00:35:40.708 --> 00:35:43.833
If there's a good offer on the table,
I am ready to make a quick deal.

399
00:35:45.167 --> 00:35:46.917
What is this? A langur.

400
00:35:47.875 --> 00:35:49.542
No. A monkey.

401
00:35:51.792 --> 00:35:53.152
Now, show me one of your pictures.

402
00:35:56.917 --> 00:35:58.458
- This one…
- Okay…

403
00:36:02.500 --> 00:36:03.750
When did I make this?

404
00:36:05.125 --> 00:36:06.125
Show me.

405
00:36:09.583 --> 00:36:11.250
Did you go near the ruins?

406
00:36:12.333 --> 00:36:14.542
Ruins? No.

407
00:36:14.833 --> 00:36:16.083
Then how did you make this?

408
00:36:16.958 --> 00:36:18.292
That's where this tree is.

409
00:36:18.917 --> 00:36:23.000
The chances of getting
a good offer are quite slim, sister.

410
00:36:24.083 --> 00:36:28.333
- What do you mean?
- Selling a house in this village is tough.

411
00:36:28.417 --> 00:36:30.500
- Are you getting it?
- Hey! What are you saying?

412
00:36:30.625 --> 00:36:32.375
You said something else to me.

413
00:36:32.708 --> 00:36:34.434
And now you're telling
daughter-in-law a different story.

414
00:36:34.458 --> 00:36:36.292
Chief, it's not me,

415
00:36:36.375 --> 00:36:37.768
people from all the villages say this.

416
00:36:37.792 --> 00:36:38.792
What do they say?

417
00:36:39.417 --> 00:36:41.500
They say this manor is cursed.

418
00:36:41.583 --> 00:36:42.583
Shut up.

419
00:36:42.708 --> 00:36:44.250
Those people even say

420
00:36:44.375 --> 00:36:46.708
that a witch in your village
devours children.

421
00:36:46.833 --> 00:36:47.708
- Is that true?
- Yes.

422
00:36:47.792 --> 00:36:49.583
Shut up. Don't talk nonsense.

423
00:36:50.125 --> 00:36:51.458
Can you show me that place?

424
00:36:51.958 --> 00:36:55.875
No, sister. I'll get a scolding.
No one goes there.

425
00:36:56.500 --> 00:36:57.375
Why?

426
00:36:57.458 --> 00:37:01.000
Everyone says it's the
dwelling place of the <i>Daitya.</i>

427
00:37:01.750 --> 00:37:04.917
- Who?
<i>- Daitya. </i>The demon!

428
00:37:05.000 --> 00:37:06.667
Daughter-in-law, it's all nonsense.

429
00:37:07.083 --> 00:37:08.167
Don't believe all this.

430
00:37:08.250 --> 00:37:09.333
- But, Chief…
- Quiet.

431
00:37:10.417 --> 00:37:13.083
I know it's all just a show
to bring the price down.

432
00:37:13.167 --> 00:37:15.184
- Not at all. That's not the case, sister.
- Leave. Leave now.

433
00:37:15.208 --> 00:37:17.083
- I said leave. Leave now. Go.
- Sister…

434
00:37:20.833 --> 00:37:23.125
Don't worry, daughter-in-law.
I am the village chief.

435
00:37:23.208 --> 00:37:24.833
This village is my responsibility.

436
00:37:25.250 --> 00:37:28.208
I will get it done.
I will find another broker.

437
00:37:29.875 --> 00:37:31.042
Who are those people?

438
00:37:32.167 --> 00:37:33.167
Hey…

439
00:37:33.250 --> 00:37:37.042
They never saw Shuvankar's family before.

440
00:37:38.208 --> 00:37:39.208
I'll deal with it.

441
00:37:39.500 --> 00:37:41.667
What?
What are you all looking at? Leave.

442
00:37:42.167 --> 00:37:45.458
<i>Daitya </i>only exists in stories
and not in real life.

443
00:37:45.750 --> 00:37:47.500
Now show me where this tree is.

444
00:37:47.583 --> 00:37:49.708
No, sister, you don't understand.

445
00:37:49.792 --> 00:37:51.352
It's okay, we'll watch from a distance.

446
00:37:51.417 --> 00:37:52.518
- We won't go near it.
- No, no…

447
00:37:52.542 --> 00:37:53.542
Deepu, come quickly.

448
00:38:03.125 --> 00:38:04.205
Do we have to go from here?

449
00:38:06.125 --> 00:38:08.125
The ruins are right behind the manor.

450
00:38:08.375 --> 00:38:09.833
The jungle can be seen from there.

451
00:38:10.125 --> 00:38:11.333
Is this a fair?

452
00:38:12.500 --> 00:38:13.500
Go home, everyone.

453
00:38:15.667 --> 00:38:16.958
Go on. Nothing to see here.

454
00:38:17.750 --> 00:38:19.875
Hey, go. Come on.

455
00:38:20.333 --> 00:38:22.292
Come, move it.

456
00:38:22.875 --> 00:38:24.542
Go on. Go.

457
00:38:48.292 --> 00:38:50.958
Over there. That's the tree.

458
00:38:58.708 --> 00:38:59.708
Come on.

459
00:39:05.333 --> 00:39:06.333
What happened?

460
00:39:06.667 --> 00:39:07.667
Why are you scared?

461
00:39:08.083 --> 00:39:09.364
We're only going to take a look.

462
00:39:09.417 --> 00:39:11.958
No, sister. We cannot go further.

463
00:39:12.417 --> 00:39:13.667
The <i>Daitya </i>will see us.

464
00:39:14.833 --> 00:39:15.833
Come on.

465
00:39:16.000 --> 00:39:18.500
You go and take a look.
I feel safer over here.

466
00:40:24.500 --> 00:40:25.625
I warned you.

467
00:40:26.500 --> 00:40:29.333
So did I. But she didn't listen.

468
00:40:30.500 --> 00:40:32.750
I only came to see that tree.

469
00:40:33.833 --> 00:40:35.917
Let's go from here. Come on.

470
00:41:17.583 --> 00:41:19.750
- Mom, let's go.
- You go I am coming.

471
00:41:38.333 --> 00:41:39.854
I looked all over the village for you.

472
00:41:40.250 --> 00:41:41.250
Why did you come here?

473
00:41:42.250 --> 00:41:44.250
Normally, you stay
glued to me all day.

474
00:41:44.375 --> 00:41:45.375
What changed today?

475
00:41:47.167 --> 00:41:48.351
The city stuff's gone to your head.

476
00:41:48.375 --> 00:41:50.625
- Come on.
- My stomach's hurting, Mom.

477
00:41:50.833 --> 00:41:52.083
Stop making excuses, Deepu.

478
00:41:52.333 --> 00:41:53.708
- Let's go home.
- Nandini.

479
00:41:57.500 --> 00:41:59.220
Your daughter's stepping
into womanhood now.

480
00:41:59.833 --> 00:42:00.833
Congratulations.

481
00:42:12.750 --> 00:42:14.500
Protect us Goddess Kali.

482
00:42:15.333 --> 00:42:18.042
Protect us Goddess Kali.
Oh, Goddess Kali…

483
00:42:18.375 --> 00:42:20.500
Did Deepika get her period, Mom?

484
00:42:21.417 --> 00:42:22.417
Yes.

485
00:42:23.167 --> 00:42:25.792
Then why is her mom so angry?

486
00:42:27.667 --> 00:42:28.667
Just forget it.

487
00:42:29.167 --> 00:42:31.625
We'll celebrate when you get your period.

488
00:42:32.583 --> 00:42:34.417
Who celebrates periods?

489
00:42:34.708 --> 00:42:37.000
There are several countries
in the world that do.

490
00:42:37.292 --> 00:42:39.667
And it's an old tradition in our country.

491
00:42:40.708 --> 00:42:42.250
When will I get my period?

492
00:42:43.625 --> 00:42:45.083
You have turned 12 now.

493
00:42:45.167 --> 00:42:46.917
So… almost there.

494
00:42:50.875 --> 00:42:51.875
Glory to Goddess Kali.

495
00:42:52.042 --> 00:42:53.042
Protect us, Goddess.

496
00:42:53.708 --> 00:42:55.625
Glory to Goddess Kali.
Protect us, Goddess.

497
00:42:55.708 --> 00:42:58.917
- Mom, my eyes are burning.
- Protect us…

498
00:42:59.417 --> 00:43:00.417
Close your eyes.

499
00:43:01.083 --> 00:43:02.324
Don't you dare open the window!

500
00:43:03.083 --> 00:43:04.833
Sit quietly. I'll be back soon.

501
00:43:05.500 --> 00:43:08.875
Protect us, Goddess Kali.
Protect us…

502
00:45:19.500 --> 00:45:20.542
Mom.

503
00:45:21.458 --> 00:45:22.458
Mom.

504
00:45:24.792 --> 00:45:27.458
Mom!

505
00:45:30.417 --> 00:45:31.417
Deepu!

506
00:45:39.417 --> 00:45:40.417
Deepu.

507
00:45:40.958 --> 00:45:41.958
Deepu.

508
00:45:42.375 --> 00:45:43.375
Deepu.

509
00:45:43.833 --> 00:45:44.833
Deepu!

510
00:45:45.458 --> 00:45:46.458
Deepu!

511
00:45:47.042 --> 00:45:48.042
Deepu!

512
00:45:48.625 --> 00:45:49.625
Deepu.

513
00:45:50.292 --> 00:45:51.167
Deepu!

514
00:45:51.250 --> 00:45:53.458
- Deepu!
- What happened, Bikash <i>da?</i>

515
00:45:54.333 --> 00:45:57.542
Deepika is not in her room, sister.

516
00:45:58.375 --> 00:46:00.458
She must be in one
of the other rooms then.

517
00:46:00.542 --> 00:46:01.833
<i>Daitya </i>took her.

518
00:46:03.000 --> 00:46:05.417
Amsaja took my Deepu.

519
00:46:05.500 --> 00:46:06.750
What nonsense, Nandini!

520
00:46:07.083 --> 00:46:09.004
Look properly.
Look in one of the adjacent rooms.

521
00:46:09.083 --> 00:46:10.458
- There are so many rooms…
- Sister,

522
00:46:10.542 --> 00:46:13.458
Deepu never goes anywhere
without telling us first.

523
00:46:14.458 --> 00:46:15.833
He took her.

524
00:46:16.000 --> 00:46:17.750
Our daughter…

525
00:46:19.333 --> 00:46:21.292
Our daughter.

526
00:46:22.208 --> 00:46:24.542
This is your fault.

527
00:46:25.333 --> 00:46:27.833
This is Shuvankar <i>da's</i> fault.

528
00:46:28.708 --> 00:46:30.208
Why did you even come here?

529
00:46:30.292 --> 00:46:32.417
- What are you saying?
- Quiet! Zip it!

530
00:46:32.667 --> 00:46:35.250
Deepu never wanders near the ruins.

531
00:46:35.333 --> 00:46:36.875
She made her go there.

532
00:46:37.792 --> 00:46:41.000
And the <i>Daitya </i>saw my Deepu.

533
00:46:44.958 --> 00:46:46.125
My Deepu.

534
00:46:48.792 --> 00:46:50.458
He must have seen you as well.

535
00:46:52.417 --> 00:46:54.292
He will come for you too.
Just wait and watch.

536
00:46:54.375 --> 00:46:56.125
- He will take you too...
- Enough, Nandini.

537
00:46:57.000 --> 00:46:58.958
Bikash <i>da,</i> control her.
She is talking nonsense.

538
00:46:59.042 --> 00:47:00.042
Quiet. Quiet.

539
00:47:00.208 --> 00:47:02.129
- Go inside. Just go.
- Since you two arrived here,

540
00:47:02.208 --> 00:47:03.649
terrible things have been happening.

541
00:47:03.917 --> 00:47:05.292
I wonder…

542
00:47:05.375 --> 00:47:08.667
- We will find her. Come on.
- What that <i>Daitya </i>is doing with my Deepu!

543
00:47:09.417 --> 00:47:13.042
This manor is cursed.
You ruined everything.

544
00:47:33.750 --> 00:47:34.750
Come.

545
00:47:36.042 --> 00:47:37.792
Daughter-in-law, meet Shekhar.

546
00:47:37.917 --> 00:47:39.417
Chandarpur Police Station in-charge.

547
00:47:39.625 --> 00:47:40.893
He will carry out the investigation.

548
00:47:40.917 --> 00:47:42.101
- Hello.
- And she is my daughter-in-law.

549
00:47:42.125 --> 00:47:43.167
Ambika Das Gupta.

550
00:47:43.458 --> 00:47:45.167
Shuvankar's wife.

551
00:47:48.250 --> 00:47:49.451
I am very sorry for your loss.

552
00:47:50.792 --> 00:47:53.250
- Thank you.
- I took command ten days ago.

553
00:47:54.708 --> 00:47:55.708
Right.

554
00:47:56.250 --> 00:47:58.333
Their daughter's name is Deepika.

555
00:47:58.708 --> 00:48:00.189
And she has been missing for an hour.

556
00:48:01.042 --> 00:48:02.442
Can you tell me from the beginning?

557
00:48:05.333 --> 00:48:08.042
Don't worry. We will do our best.

558
00:48:13.958 --> 00:48:15.542
Whoever entered used the window…

559
00:48:16.917 --> 00:48:18.000
And took the child.

560
00:48:19.292 --> 00:48:21.667
But he should have
left footprints in the soil,

561
00:48:22.917 --> 00:48:23.917
which are missing.

562
00:48:25.292 --> 00:48:27.625
<i>Daitya </i>doesn't have footprints.

563
00:48:28.958 --> 00:48:29.958
<i>Daitya?</i>

564
00:48:30.833 --> 00:48:31.833
The demon.

565
00:48:32.500 --> 00:48:33.500
Demon?

566
00:48:37.083 --> 00:48:38.268
Did a demon enter the village?

567
00:48:38.292 --> 00:48:40.167
- Yes! Yes!
- Yes!

568
00:48:41.208 --> 00:48:42.292
I am not lying.

569
00:48:44.292 --> 00:48:47.625
Deepu is not the first girl to disappear.

570
00:48:48.958 --> 00:48:52.875
In this village,
any girl who gets her first period,

571
00:48:53.542 --> 00:48:55.208
<i>Daitya </i>takes her to the jungle.

572
00:48:58.958 --> 00:49:00.875
- Village Chief.
- Yes.

573
00:49:01.042 --> 00:49:02.417
Did you know about this?

574
00:49:04.333 --> 00:49:05.417
Well, actually...

575
00:49:05.500 --> 00:49:06.820
How long has this been happening?

576
00:49:07.333 --> 00:49:08.333
Daughter-in-law,

577
00:49:08.833 --> 00:49:12.542
girls have been disappearing
for the last three to four months.

578
00:49:12.875 --> 00:49:14.625
- But...
- Hold on a second.

579
00:49:14.958 --> 00:49:16.809
Not a single case has been registered
at the police station about this.

580
00:49:16.833 --> 00:49:17.833
How can it be registered?

581
00:49:17.917 --> 00:49:19.667
Girls disappear,

582
00:49:20.417 --> 00:49:24.583
but they return home safe
and sound after a couple of days.

583
00:49:25.583 --> 00:49:26.875
How can we file a case?

584
00:49:27.250 --> 00:49:28.375
There is no problem.

585
00:49:28.708 --> 00:49:30.583
There is a problem, Village Chief.

586
00:49:30.667 --> 00:49:32.000
Her daughter is the problem!

587
00:49:32.083 --> 00:49:33.476
- What are you saying?
- Even you know this.

588
00:49:33.500 --> 00:49:35.167
Have you all lost your minds?

589
00:49:35.375 --> 00:49:36.375
Everyone, quiet.

590
00:49:36.417 --> 00:49:37.417
Joydev.

591
00:49:38.000 --> 00:49:42.750
Three months ago,
both the men in their family died.

592
00:49:43.125 --> 00:49:46.000
Since then,
Amsaja has been coming here

593
00:49:46.292 --> 00:49:48.917
and bothering the girls of this village.

594
00:49:49.000 --> 00:49:52.667
- Yes, it's true. It's true.
- What are you all saying?

595
00:49:52.750 --> 00:49:54.625
- Yes, it's true.
- Everyone, quiet.

596
00:49:54.708 --> 00:49:56.875
You all couldn't protect your daughters,

597
00:49:57.708 --> 00:50:00.250
so you are easily blaming my daughter.

598
00:50:00.417 --> 00:50:01.333
No, daughter-in-law...

599
00:50:01.417 --> 00:50:03.377
There is no difference
between Shweta and Deepika.

600
00:50:04.083 --> 00:50:06.917
And if you think Deepika
was taken by the<i> Daitya,</i>

601
00:50:07.833 --> 00:50:09.954
then I am willing to go
to the jungle to get her back.

602
00:50:10.292 --> 00:50:11.792
Yes, Nandini, will you go with me?

603
00:50:12.625 --> 00:50:13.625
Daughter-in-law.

604
00:50:15.833 --> 00:50:18.708
It won't be right to go to the jungle.

605
00:50:19.542 --> 00:50:24.167
Das Babu's son went there
looking for his daughter.

606
00:50:25.167 --> 00:50:26.250
His daughter came home,

607
00:50:27.333 --> 00:50:28.574
but he hasn't returned to date.

608
00:50:30.000 --> 00:50:31.280
Not the jungle, daughter-in-law.

609
00:50:46.250 --> 00:50:48.292
Daughter-in-law, listen to me.

610
00:50:48.750 --> 00:50:51.333
The jungle is infested
with wild animals at night.

611
00:50:51.917 --> 00:50:52.917
Don't go there.

612
00:50:53.208 --> 00:50:57.125
Daughter-in-law, I will call
the forest department tomorrow.

613
00:50:57.625 --> 00:50:59.333
It's a police case now, Chief.

614
00:51:01.375 --> 00:51:02.667
I will deal with your <i>Daitya.</i>

615
00:51:02.917 --> 00:51:04.500
- But…
- Chief,

616
00:51:04.708 --> 00:51:07.333
if you are scared, then stay here.

617
00:51:08.333 --> 00:51:09.333
Alright.

618
00:52:31.375 --> 00:52:32.375
Deepika.

619
00:52:35.750 --> 00:52:36.750
Deepika.

620
00:52:38.917 --> 00:52:39.917
That way.

621
00:52:45.125 --> 00:52:46.125
Deepika.

622
00:52:48.958 --> 00:52:49.958
Deepika.

623
00:53:03.917 --> 00:53:04.917
Deepika?

624
00:53:49.250 --> 00:53:50.292
Deepika.

625
00:55:19.500 --> 00:55:20.500
Ambika ma'am.

626
00:55:24.583 --> 00:55:25.583
Are you alright?

627
00:55:29.208 --> 00:55:30.500
Sorry, I lost my way.

628
00:55:32.750 --> 00:55:35.875
Did you hear the sound
of children crying?

629
00:55:37.833 --> 00:55:39.042
It's completely silent here.

630
00:55:41.458 --> 00:55:42.667
We should leave, Ambika ma'am.

631
00:55:42.917 --> 00:55:44.417
I don't think Deepika is here.

632
00:55:46.000 --> 00:55:47.000
Come.

633
00:56:06.167 --> 00:56:07.167
Shweta.

634
00:56:10.583 --> 00:56:12.542
Thank God you are safe, Mom.

635
00:56:14.417 --> 00:56:15.833
Relax, dear.

636
00:56:17.083 --> 00:56:18.083
I am okay.

637
00:56:18.583 --> 00:56:19.583
Did you find Deepika?

638
00:56:22.458 --> 00:56:25.500
No, but she will be found.

639
00:56:28.625 --> 00:56:29.625
Do you know…

640
00:56:29.792 --> 00:56:34.708
People were saying
all this was Dad's fault.

641
00:56:35.833 --> 00:56:37.625
That demon came for me

642
00:56:38.792 --> 00:56:40.458
but took Deepika.

643
00:56:42.042 --> 00:56:43.917
The demon is called Amsaja.

644
00:56:44.250 --> 00:56:45.250
Right?

645
00:56:49.750 --> 00:56:51.667
Amsaja is just a story.

646
00:56:52.833 --> 00:56:56.583
A myth that the villagers
of Chandarpur fear.

647
00:56:58.333 --> 00:57:00.292
Don't believe them.

648
00:57:02.375 --> 00:57:03.458
I won't, Mom.

649
00:57:04.458 --> 00:57:08.375
Just tell me why you
and Dad would make excuses

650
00:57:08.708 --> 00:57:11.583
whenever the topic
of Chandarpur came up.

651
00:57:12.458 --> 00:57:14.333
Why did you two always lie?

652
00:57:16.292 --> 00:57:18.042
What are you hiding from me, Mom?

653
00:57:20.708 --> 00:57:21.917
I am so sorry, dear.

654
00:57:24.708 --> 00:57:25.958
I won't hide anything today.

655
00:57:28.292 --> 00:57:29.542
Even your dad wanted…

656
00:57:31.708 --> 00:57:33.042
You to find out everything.

657
00:57:34.333 --> 00:57:35.333
What is it?

658
00:57:38.083 --> 00:57:41.042
Do you remember the painting
of the seven Goddesses?

659
00:57:42.792 --> 00:57:44.333
The one of Goddess Kali
and Raktabij?

660
00:57:46.292 --> 00:57:47.833
Yes, I remember.

661
00:57:50.625 --> 00:57:53.083
The people of Chandarpur believe…

662
00:57:54.417 --> 00:57:56.458
Raktabij's story did not end there.

663
00:57:58.000 --> 00:58:00.208
<i>Raktabij was indeed killed in the war,</i>

664
00:58:01.167 --> 00:58:04.208
<i>but a drop of his blood
fell on Earth.</i>

665
00:58:06.458 --> 00:58:08.000
<i>And a new demon was born.</i>

666
00:58:08.333 --> 00:58:09.333
<i>Amsaja.</i>

667
00:58:17.167 --> 00:58:18.917
The place where
the drop of blood fell

668
00:58:20.333 --> 00:58:21.333
is this.

669
00:58:21.958 --> 00:58:22.958
Chandarpur.

670
00:58:25.208 --> 00:58:27.958
Amsaja couldn't spawn
new demons from his own blood.

671
00:58:28.583 --> 00:58:30.833
And he couldn't defeat
Goddess Kali alone.

672
00:58:32.417 --> 00:58:34.208
So to fulfill his motive,

673
00:58:34.833 --> 00:58:37.750
he laid his foul eyes on humans.

674
00:58:38.667 --> 00:58:41.625
<i>He began abducting
the daughters of Chandarpur,</i>

675
00:58:42.417 --> 00:58:44.583
<i>because he wanted
to create new demons.</i>

676
00:58:44.708 --> 00:58:47.333
<i>But none of the girls
could withstand him.</i>

677
00:58:49.542 --> 00:58:52.750
Several daughters from
the village fell prey to Amsaja.

678
00:58:54.167 --> 00:58:55.708
The village was gripped
with mourning.

679
00:58:57.750 --> 00:58:58.750
Then…

680
00:58:59.542 --> 00:59:02.833
One of Goddess Kali's
devotees prayed for help.

681
00:59:04.583 --> 00:59:05.784
She showered her divine mercy.

682
00:59:09.417 --> 00:59:14.917
<i>And a drop of blood fell from Goddess
Kali's statue into the devotee's eye.</i>

683
00:59:15.875 --> 00:59:17.833
<i>He was blessed with limitless powers.</i>

684
00:59:18.667 --> 00:59:20.417
<i>He could defeat Amsaja now.</i>

685
00:59:21.167 --> 00:59:23.458
<i>But Amsaja suddenly disappeared.</i>

686
00:59:24.333 --> 00:59:26.375
<i>Everyone thought we'd won.</i>

687
00:59:26.792 --> 00:59:27.832
<i>But that was not the case.</i>

688
00:59:28.500 --> 00:59:31.292
<i>He was simply waiting.</i>

689
00:59:31.792 --> 00:59:33.292
<i>Waiting for what?</i>

690
00:59:33.708 --> 00:59:37.083
Amsaja knew the devotee was blessed
by Goddess Kali's powers.

691
00:59:39.125 --> 00:59:40.542
When he had a daughter,

692
00:59:40.917 --> 00:59:42.500
the powers were transferred to her.

693
00:59:46.000 --> 00:59:48.333
Now Amsaja could fulfill his motive.

694
00:59:49.667 --> 00:59:50.667
He knew…

695
00:59:51.875 --> 00:59:54.458
That only that girl
could take his legacy forward.

696
00:59:55.125 --> 00:59:56.500
<i>When she turned 12,</i>

697
00:59:57.333 --> 00:59:59.958
<i>Amsaja came back and abducted her.</i>

698
01:00:00.875 --> 01:00:04.167
<i>When she was found,
she was pregnant with the demon's child.</i>

699
01:00:04.875 --> 01:00:08.667
<i>Amsaja had put the girl's father
in a strange dilemma.</i>

700
01:00:09.667 --> 01:00:11.250
If the child had been born,

701
01:00:12.250 --> 01:00:13.500
Amsaja would have won.

702
01:00:15.417 --> 01:00:16.537
To stop that from happening,

703
01:00:17.708 --> 01:00:22.917
the girl's father did
what no father could imagine.

704
01:00:25.000 --> 01:00:26.000
What did he do?

705
01:00:27.708 --> 01:00:29.708
<i>He sacrificed his own daughter.</i>

706
01:00:33.583 --> 01:00:35.750
It's a really horrifying story, Mom.

707
01:00:36.458 --> 01:00:39.417
But how is it connected to us?

708
01:00:45.333 --> 01:00:47.167
Everyone in Chandarpur believes…

709
01:00:49.250 --> 01:00:55.042
That Shuvankar's family are the
descendants of that powerful devotee.

710
01:00:56.833 --> 01:00:57.875
Our family.

711
01:00:59.708 --> 01:01:00.958
Are you serious?

712
01:01:05.292 --> 01:01:06.333
And because of this fear,

713
01:01:06.875 --> 01:01:09.417
whenever a daughter
is born in this family,

714
01:01:10.750 --> 01:01:15.250
they are sacrificed
on the first Kali puja.

715
01:01:26.083 --> 01:01:30.458
Even I… am a daughter of this family.

716
01:01:32.125 --> 01:01:35.250
Your father never
believed in such stories.

717
01:01:35.875 --> 01:01:38.833
In fact, when he came
to Kolkata to study,

718
01:01:39.542 --> 01:01:44.000
he decided never
to return to Chandarpur.

719
01:01:45.833 --> 01:01:48.625
<i>Away from your grandpa
and this village,</i>

720
01:01:49.292 --> 01:01:53.042
<i>we built our own safe, little world.</i>

721
01:01:55.292 --> 01:01:56.292
Shweta.

722
01:02:22.042 --> 01:02:23.667
Father, come in.

723
01:02:26.917 --> 01:02:27.917
It's a boy.

724
01:02:31.750 --> 01:02:33.292
Glory to Goddess Kali.

725
01:02:33.917 --> 01:02:35.542
Thank you very much.

726
01:03:01.417 --> 01:03:06.167
We had broken a sacrificial tradition
that had been followed for centuries.

727
01:03:08.167 --> 01:03:09.167
So, that means…

728
01:03:09.917 --> 01:03:13.542
The imaginary demon cannot harm me.

729
01:03:14.250 --> 01:03:15.250
Right, Mom?

730
01:03:16.625 --> 01:03:18.417
As long as your mom is with you,

731
01:03:21.333 --> 01:03:23.042
no one can harm you.

732
01:04:41.958 --> 01:04:43.292
Hey, Batul<i> da.</i>

733
01:04:43.583 --> 01:04:47.333
- Village Chief. Hello.
- Hello.

734
01:04:47.417 --> 01:04:48.958
- What brings you here?
- All good?

735
01:04:49.042 --> 01:04:50.042
Yes.

736
01:04:50.417 --> 01:04:52.292
- Is your daughter at home?
- Yes, she is.

737
01:04:52.917 --> 01:04:54.684
The inspector needs
to ask her some questions.

738
01:04:54.708 --> 01:04:55.708
I see.

739
01:04:56.417 --> 01:04:58.097
Do you remember where
you were taken, dear?

740
01:04:58.542 --> 01:05:00.125
Did you hear anything unusual?

741
01:05:03.333 --> 01:05:04.333
Speak up.

742
01:05:05.042 --> 01:05:06.042
Did you see anything?

743
01:05:06.792 --> 01:05:07.792
No.

744
01:05:07.833 --> 01:05:09.542
Do you remember who took you there?

745
01:05:25.167 --> 01:05:26.607
<i>None of the girls remember anything.</i>

746
01:05:27.750 --> 01:05:30.083
Who took them, where they were taken,

747
01:05:31.958 --> 01:05:32.958
what happened with them…

748
01:05:33.833 --> 01:05:36.792
There is one child
who saw an old woman.

749
01:05:40.833 --> 01:05:43.917
Daughter-in-law,
I fully suspect that old woman.

750
01:05:44.708 --> 01:05:46.125
She knows black magic.

751
01:05:47.292 --> 01:05:51.458
That's why she was exiled
from the village forty years ago.

752
01:05:52.000 --> 01:05:53.881
A couple of people have
seen her in the village.

753
01:05:54.167 --> 01:05:55.667
And these events started after that.

754
01:05:55.833 --> 01:05:57.708
Which means she is behind them, right?

755
01:06:21.083 --> 01:06:22.083
Shweta.

756
01:06:24.208 --> 01:06:25.208
Shweta.

757
01:06:29.250 --> 01:06:30.250
Shweta.

758
01:06:31.708 --> 01:06:36.250
He left. Your husband left everyone.

759
01:06:36.333 --> 01:06:37.208
He left.

760
01:06:37.292 --> 01:06:39.958
Shuvankar just left us all behind.

761
01:06:40.708 --> 01:06:44.708
Your father. He left everything.

762
01:06:44.792 --> 01:06:46.500
He… Right here…

763
01:06:47.042 --> 01:06:49.708
He used to sit right here

764
01:06:50.583 --> 01:06:53.083
and hear stories of the <i>Daitya.</i>

765
01:06:55.542 --> 01:06:57.250
<i>Daitya's </i>stories.

766
01:06:58.292 --> 01:06:59.292
He would get scared.

767
01:07:00.667 --> 01:07:03.667
Mom, he was telling me about Dad.

768
01:07:04.958 --> 01:07:05.958
Come.

769
01:07:11.000 --> 01:07:12.000
Take this.

770
01:07:15.958 --> 01:07:17.292
It belongs to Shuvankar.

771
01:07:20.042 --> 01:07:21.458
It bears the Goddess's command.

772
01:07:33.042 --> 01:07:36.917
"When the demon

773
01:07:37.708 --> 01:07:41.250
will spread its sins,

774
01:07:42.542 --> 01:07:46.417
the tears of the daughter will

775
01:07:47.792 --> 01:07:51.833
seep into the soil as blood,

776
01:07:53.542 --> 01:07:58.958
the scepter of the Goddess
will be the biggest boon,

777
01:08:00.750 --> 01:08:06.083
the blood of the daughter will

778
01:08:07.125 --> 01:08:11.708
"annihilate the demon."

779
01:08:37.833 --> 01:08:40.542
When the demon will spread its sins,

780
01:08:42.292 --> 01:08:45.708
the tears of the daughter will seep
into the soil as blood,

781
01:08:46.250 --> 01:08:48.417
the scepter of the Goddess
will be the biggest boon,

782
01:08:49.208 --> 01:08:52.958
the blood of the daughter
will annihilate the demon.

783
01:09:29.542 --> 01:09:32.792
<i>When the demon will spread its sins,
